(Bug #81, the other half: the hole parser split off the format spec at the
 first `:` it saw, including one inside the quoted key, so `{scores's \"a:b\"}`
 was read as the empty key and quietly returned the wrong value. The hole
 parser is shared by every site that takes a format string, so the quoted key
 is checked here at each of them, and against the specs it composes with.)

a map called scores is {"ada": 10, "a:b": 5}.
a text called player is "ada".

(A key with a colon in it belongs to the key, not to the format spec.)
Print "colon in the key: {scores's \"a:b\"}".

(A spec after a quoted key is still a spec, either spelling of the key.)
Print "padded dynamic: [{scores's \"{player}\":6}]".
Print "padded static: [{scores's \"ada\":6}]".
Print "hex: {scores's \"{player}\":x}".

(The same hole, at each site that takes a format string.)
a text called line is "as a text value: {scores's \"{player}\"}".
Print line.

a buffer called note is 64 bytes in size.
Append "into a buffer: {scores's \"{player}\"}" to note.
Print note.

a list called lines is ["in a list: {scores's \"{player}\"}"].
Print lines's first.
